ve.\n\nReason: The pot is small because no one has bet. My hand is weak—just a pair of tens with poor kickers. I have no strong draw. Checking allows me to see the river for free and possibly improve to two pair or trips (though unlikely). If I raise, I risk being called or raised by a stronger hand, and I don’t have enough equity to justify betting for value. Folding would be too tight since I have a pair and it costs nothing to check. So the best move is to check and hope to improve on the river or bluff later if a scare card comes.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
